; QEMU's riscv64 virt board's devices, the one table of them: each line a
; base, a length, the name tests/virt/board calls it, board_NAME, or - for
; none, and what it is. tools/boards.l0 writes virt-riscv64-devices.ll and
; tests/virt/board/virt-riscv64-devices.l0 from it, and spec
; boards/virt-riscv64.md lists the same. tools/test.sh --virt fails when
; either written file is not what this table gives.
0x10000000 0x100 uart the 16550
0x00101000 0x1000 rtc the goldfish RTC
0x10100000 0x18 fw_cfg firmware configuration
0x10001000 0x8000 virtio 8 virtio-mmio transports
